From 0e6bef9a800d3190bbce977dc26bd4dede9a4602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:28:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(post): comment the setup, operation and tool in
 posted programs

Every built-in post now writes, in its own comment syntax, the setup
name where its first section opens, each operation's name, kind and
work offset at its preamble, and each tool's number, name, kind,
diameter and corner radius just ahead of its tool call. Only comment
lines are added; no motion changes.

post::dump carries four new optional PARAMs for this (OperationKind,
SetupName, ToolKind, ToolCornerRadius), each written only when stated,
so legacy streams and user scripts read as before. User text is cleaned
per dialect: ASCII only, capped at 40 characters, and ( ) % ; (plus *
on Heidenhain) never reach a comment.

Refs #257

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
